// this variant assumes open types can be enumerated when the domain (is made) finite

Open Fact unbounded Identified by Int

Fact created Identified by Int

Event add_single Related to int
  Creates created(int) When unbounded(int)

Event add_multiple
  Creates created(unbounded) When unbounded.

Extend Fact unbounded Identified by 1..7.

// enumeration happens here, gives no exceptions under simpler treatment of open types
-unbounded.
+unbounded(5).

add_single(5).
?!created(1).
?!created(3).
?created(5).
?!created(7).

add_multiple().

?!created(1).
?!created(3).
?created(5).
?!created(7).

// enumeration happens here, gives no exceptions under simpler treatment of open types
+unbounded When unbounded % 2 == 1.

add_multiple().

?created(1).
?created(3).
?created(5).
?created(7).
